# hunting-grounds.vrs: hunting-grounds D21 (Session 2). hg-roam (a Region location over FarbaneWoods, the lock on, no
# behaviour, two waves of 10 CHAR_Spider_Forest 30 s apart) logs each wave "in <g> groups over FarbaneWoods" with g of 2
# or more and one verbose spot line per group. The spots are then visited one by one (a second run written from those
# spot lines: `.devtp` there, `.nyar region here`, `.nyar debug here 15`), and the 30 m spacing is read from them.
# Needs: the step 3 Release DLL; NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devgo, .devmark, .devhop) and DevChatEcho; the dev events.json
# entries hg-roam, hg-lock, hg-ambush, hg-point, hg-timing (docs/features/HUNTING_GROUNDS.md, Session 2), scope
# FarbaneWoods (the pond is in it, Session 1); [Debug] VerboseLogging = true; Chaos invulnerable
# (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false).
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .devgo pond
expect-log \[DEV TP\] pond
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .nyar region here
expect-reply you are in FarbaneWoods
mark
chat .nyar event start hg-roam
expect-log event hg-roam started by
expect-log event hg-roam wave 1/2 in [2-9] groups over FarbaneWoods: 10 units queued timeout=30
expect-log event hg-roam wave 2/2 in [2-9] groups over FarbaneWoods: 10 units queued timeout=60
wait 10
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 20
